WEBVTT

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:40.550
You say you were under threat?

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:45.560
Yes. And it was under the sort of force that would give you nightmares.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:49.890
I did not know that you were so delicate a person.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:53.300
I've never been all that good with handling the rough stuff.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:06.970
This inquiry is concluded. We will have to keep you in custody for the time being.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:17.590
Shall I check the combat records?

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:20.930
That's all right. It probably won't do any good anyhow.

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:22.260
Right...

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.260
Trying to keep a lid on this, huh?

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:28.820
The ways of the bureaucrat never change, do they?

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.540
You guys seem to have a history with those two.

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:39.710
Ever since a long time ago, there have been many occasions

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:42.210
where we've found ourselves on different sides of things.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:45.550
We've both gotten in the way of each other's work, you see.

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:49.550
I thought it was strange that we should both end up in the same organization.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:52.550
Sure enough, it appears to have been the hand of Fate at work.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:03:01.900
Very well. Un-ou, A-ou, I hereby order you to eliminate Éclair and Lumiere.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:03.920
Yes, Ma'am.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.260
This sure takes me back!

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:31.600
I wonder how many decades it has been since we were in this constellation.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:38.940
Sometimes, I envy your optimism. Right now, the whole galaxy is our enemy.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.670
Do you understand that?

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:44.680
It's all right! There isn't anybody around who knows

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.210
that we would come to a place like this.

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:48.870
Éclair...

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.550
It's a terrible sight, huh?

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:59.320
I had heard stories about it, but I had no idea...

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:22.640
<i>Éclair... That's a nice name.</i>

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.860
Reading a phase. Someone is warping out!

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:33.860
A pursuer?

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.990
That's what we have to think.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.800
I wonder how they knew about this place.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:44.870
Not even Armblast is supposed to know about it.

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:49.500
There are certain others who also have ties to this place... two of them...

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.880
The Salyut!

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:58.220
<i>You two wanted persons there, we've missed you!</i>

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.550
Un-ou!

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:02.750
This is indeed an ideal place for you to hide,

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:06.220
but you blew it when you forgot about our eyes and ears.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:11.560
Nice of you to remember this place, after however many decades it's been.

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:14.230
We haven't forgotten how you gave us such trouble.

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.900
You put us in quite a painful situation, after all.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:20.960
We'd like to forget everything about <i>you</i> as soon as we can!

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:24.710
You're not getting away!

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:35.110
Emergency warp has failed! The phase navigation device has gone irregular!

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:41.250
I'm used to the way you guys operate!

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:52.130
Why, you!

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:05.220
They're fast!

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:09.890
Their inertial control system appears to be a cut above our own!

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:12.190
They're systematically closing in on us!

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:21.790
Lumiere!

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:28.700
Lumiere...

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:37.700
Why, you!

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:42.650
This'll be interesting!

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:58.870
What's the matter?

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:03.040
The interference from the two beams has emitted quantum turbulence,

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.540
causing an overflow in our inertial control system.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:10.640
This is why I hate these latest machines! Defensive posture!

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.370
What?

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:20.380
Why? This would have been an ideal chance to attack...

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:29.230
It looks like they took a lot of damage as well.

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:32.070
All right then, we still have luck on our side!

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:12.310
Wirbelwind, how is she?

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:22.350
She won't make it on these emergency medical nanomachines alone.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:26.220
Éclair...

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:29.230
Lumiere, are you in pain?

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:34.660
No, not right now. How long does it look like I will hold out?

00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:37.790
Two hours.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:43.770
I sure have lived a long time, but now, when the end comes,

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:45.800
it's all so sudden, isn't it?

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:51.080
Éclair, would you please bring me some grape juice?

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:52.850
Huh?

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:59.190
I've hidden some vintage stuff behind panel 3A on the dogfight bridge.

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:02.860
I'd like you to share a glass with me.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:04.450
No!

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:10.160
You know better than anyone that I never know when to quit!

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:26.880
Éclair, where are we going?

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.980
To the place of promise.

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:32.360
You don't mean the one?

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:39.160
I doubt there's even a one-in-a-million hope...

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:42.830
One-in-a-million still isn't zero!

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:46.630
I really don't know what to say about that personality of yours...

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:08.690
Franz...

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:28.470
Looks like you've gotten much better.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:46.090
<i>I see. So you girls live beyond time, huh?</i>

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:58.910
I can't hear a thing. How about you?

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:10.190
No good. With this much shielding, my eyes aren't any use.

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:13.120
Those guys have seen through our methods too, huh?

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:18.860
Look at that. It's the assembly hall for this colony.

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:22.870
That's the very same hole that you opened up.

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:26.540
That should have earned us quite a bit back then.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:29.540
Rounding up the previous administration's politicians,

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:31.210
then handing them over to the coup d'état faction,

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:34.210
we would have gotten all the reward money we could have taken.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:37.210
I don't understand why our job was to capture them alive,

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:39.550
if they were just going to kill them anyway, though.

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:43.040
And yet, those guys interfered once again...

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:52.230
The wounded come first! Hurry!

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:25.160
Back then, we were mercenaries for the coup d'état faction,

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:28.600
and they were the peace officers from the central dispatch.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:31.370
Now, we're on the side of the straightlaced GOTT,

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:33.800
and they are the ones who are wanted.

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:35.870
The world is an interesting place, huh?

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:39.410
All things pass. The vicissitudes in the world of men are difficult

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:42.210
for those of us who are not gods to fathom.

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:46.810
Are you sure your speech isn't getting more and more clerical?

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:48.580
Are they there!?

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:52.890
No, just the embers of their presence.

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:54.760
Let me see, too.

00:12:57.900 --> 00:12:59.920
Have they gone out?

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:14.910
Another thirty minutes.

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:19.250
<i>If anything were to happen to Lumiere, I'd...</i>

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:20.920
Say...

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:25.120
Here like this, I'm remembering what happened back then.

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:30.890
The time when he helped you, after you had been injured...

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:47.210
You hold that side.

00:13:47.210 --> 00:13:50.550
My hospital is near here. Hurry!

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:51.910
R- right!

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:59.890
It's been so many decades since then... but it's like it was yesterday...

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:01.890
Don't talk too much.

00:14:01.890 --> 00:14:07.460
You're right. Knowing him, he just might keep his promise.

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:12.090
He might not have forgotten us, all these decades later...

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:14.430
Lumiere!

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.350
Ganador!

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:28.980
Donner!

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:58.850
Donner, look after Lumiere!

00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:05.880
You're mine!

00:15:21.570 --> 00:15:23.910
I've been waiting for this moment!

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:27.370
Nobody likes a pesky boy!

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:44.190
That's far enough!

00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:46.250
So that's what's going on.

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:53.540
Please, just wait one hour. If I don't hurry and attend to Lumiere...

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:56.540
Unfortunately, that won't be necessary.

00:15:56.540 --> 00:16:01.550
The orders we've received were not to catch you, but to eliminate you.

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:05.580
And you expect to treat her in a place like this?

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:08.550
Were you trying to find a doctor or something?

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:10.710
He promised us...

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:18.230
I see. So you girls live beyond time, huh?

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:22.230
Yes, as we change appearances over and over.

00:16:22.230 --> 00:16:26.570
In that case, I can't very well keep you any longer.

00:16:26.570 --> 00:16:30.570
I'm joking! I'm joking with you!

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:35.850
Franz, why don't you get away from here, together with us?

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:38.550
This civil war looks like it's going to drag on.

00:16:38.550 --> 00:16:41.480
You should move yourself to a safer place now, while you can.

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:46.320
Some day, when this colony is at peace...

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:49.530
once that happens, will you come here again?

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:53.200
When you do, I might be an old man.

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:55.220
Franz...

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:59.690
I know, I'll make you a promise...

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:07.340
He made us a promise that if we ever got into trouble,

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:09.550
he would always be here to help us...

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:12.380
That even if he were to pass away,

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:14.550
he would arrange for facilities that we could use...

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:18.220
And so, if we go to his hospital, I'm sure that!

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:23.230
That's absurd! How many decades do you think it's been since then?

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:27.100
You know what happened to this colony after all that, right?

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:30.230
He's sure to have forgotten about that promise right away.

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:31.540
And if he did remember it,

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:34.500
do you think he would have had enough time to faithfully keep it?

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:40.510
People who live normally are like shadows passing by to folks like us.

00:17:40.510 --> 00:17:43.650
Someone taking such great care to remember such an oral promise?

00:17:43.650 --> 00:17:46.180
I can't call that anything but stupid.

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:50.090
Yeah. Knowing you, you would think that.

00:17:50.850 --> 00:17:54.190
We've known each other a long time, huh Éclair?

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:56.560
I'll at least come and visit your grave.

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:07.760
A-ou!!

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:42.630
Is there anything you want me to do?

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:47.170
Just stay here like this.

00:18:59.190 --> 00:19:00.780
He's alive!

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:07.990
Password...

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:12.060
<i>Éclair... That's a nice name.</i>

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:15.270
Éclair...

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:33.490
It's been a long time, hasn't it, Éclair and Lumiere?

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:35.220
Franz?

00:19:36.490 --> 00:19:40.500
I wonder how many years from now it will be when you receive this message...

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:43.170
Ten years? Fifty years?

00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:46.640
It might even be much farther into the future than that.

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:48.510
Right now, as I'm recording these images,

00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:52.000
it's been three years since we parted ways.

00:19:53.180 --> 00:19:55.710
The war just keeps getting worse and worse.

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:57.850
People are dying all too easily.

00:19:57.850 --> 00:20:00.520
I don't know how long I will be safe here.

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:05.520
But I will leave you this place, for whenever you two come back here.

00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:09.650
Éclair, just as I promised you.

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:20.200
It's just about time for inspection. Farewell, Éclair.

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:24.230
May you always get along with Lumiere, and take care of yourselves.

00:20:25.880 --> 00:20:28.400
Franz, thank you...

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:49.090
Can you wait until we're finished?

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:55.170
Are you sure? This will make you traitors, too.

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:58.480
GOTT is starting to smell pretty fishy,

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:00.410
and this will make for a good opportunity to change jobs.

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:01.780
We've got some prospects, too.

00:21:05.520 --> 00:21:10.190
It's Lumiere's specially prepared anti-D-command vaccine.

00:21:10.190 --> 00:21:11.780
Éclair!

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:16.650
<i>I'm</i> going to be the one that kills you. Don't forget that.

00:23:06.910 --> 00:23:11.510
<i>What you find hidden inside hard, cold armor</i>

00:23:11.510 --> 00:23:15.250
<i>will always be something very soft, and warm.</i>

00:23:15.250 --> 00:23:19.950
<i>Next time on Kiddy Grade</i>
